# tub — the real leak (ODE)
# the drain reads the tub's OWN level: fuller -> more pressure -> leaks faster.
# that single `proportional` (instead of a flat constant) is what turns arithmetic
# into an ODE. it starts empty, fills, and settles where inflow balances outflow:
# 3 / 0.1 = 30 — a level nobody wrote down; it emerges from the balance.
node tub : range(0, 50) @ bucket
external faucet
external drain

faucet -> tub  : constant(c = 3)
tub -> drain   : proportional(k = 0.1)      # 'of' defaults to the source (tub)

pathway leaky_tub : faucet->tub, tub->drain
